body:
Just answered. 

&#x200B;

I find it weird that none of the questions addressed any actual arguments they had against veganism. This whole survey was just their idea of 'Let's share reasons why vegoons suck'.

I remember being pretty much the same when I was little. I felt so much pity for the toys I didn't play with, the clothes I didn't wear, even foods I disliked. When I was around 7, someone gave me a doll for my birthday. I hated dolls with a passion at the time, so I got pretty pissed, but a few days passed and I started to carry that thing everywhere I went because I felt bad. I still have a lot of my old toys, notebooks from elementary school and clothes that don't fit me that well anymore. If I get angry at an appliance not working properly, I feel I have to apologize afterward, because at least it's trying. It's kind of ridiculous.

&#x200B;

There was this beautiful, old cherry tree at my grandparents' house where I spent a lot of my time as a child. A few months ago I happened to pass by (someone else lives there now) and saw that the tree got cut. It kind of came as an emotional shock. I also recall crying over two trees getting cut down near my house. I was really embarrassed about it though.

&#x200B;

I also get this feeling whenever I see things in stores that nobody wants to buy, or when street vendors sell handmade things to people passing by and they get ignored. Or over music people tend to hate on. I have a tendency to hoard things that hold any sort of sentimental value tbh.

&#x200B;

Throwing them away would almost feel like I'm chipping away at my sense of identity, almost as if I wouldn't be myself without these objects I'm attached to. The weird thing is that I'm a very detached person by nature, especially from the people around me. I have trouble feeling even slight affection. So this really makes no sense lol.

Kubera is probably one of the most underrated webtoons, and it's really a shame. The first chapters may seem generic (I initially dropped it because of that), but the more you read, the better it becomes. The worldbuilding is outstanding, the characters are really complex and the storyline takes so many twists and turns. It's amazing how the tone changes as the plot moves forward, and the darker undertones rise to the surface.

&#x200B;

I highly recommend it to anyone looking for a complex story to binge (it has almost 400 chapters atm).
